          "content": "The redesign is complete, type-checks, and lints clean. Here's what I changed — all confined to the Step 4 (Rooms & rates) UI in `components/partner/property-setup.tsx`, using only existing APIs.\n\n## UX fixes\n\n**Guided accordion instead of three stacked forms.** The room / policy / rate forms are now collapsible panels (`AddPanel`). Only the relevant one is open at a time; after you save a room it auto-advances to the policy step, then to the rate step. Disabled steps are dimmed and can't be opened out of order. This removes the long, overwhelming scroll from your screenshots.\n\n**Forms reset after saving.** Each form remounts via a `formNonce` key on success, so completed sections don't linger with stale input.\n\n**A real progress checklist** at the top (Room type / Cancellation policy / Sellable rate) shows exactly what's done and what's missing, with live counts.\n\n**Better notices.** Success/error/info now render with distinct colors and proper `role=\"status\"`/`role=\"alert\"` instead of a plain gray box.\n\n## New feature: full detail view\n\nReplaced the count-only `Summary` tiles (`ROOM TYPES 1 Deluxe`, etc.) with rich detail cards:\n\n- **Room cards** (`RoomDetailCard`): name, description, max guests, rooms-to-sell, a Sellable/Needs-a-rate badge, and a nested list of that room's rates — each rate showing its name, the linked cancellation policy, and the formatted per-night price (via `formatPaise`). Each card has an inline \"Add rate\" shortcut that opens the rate panel pre-selected to that room.\n- **Policy cards** (`PolicyDetailCard`): name, description, free-cancellation window (\"Free until 24h before check-in\"), and the fee (or \"No cancellation fee\").\n- Empty state when no rooms exist yet.\n\nNow everything you create is fully visible and cross-referenced, not just a number.\n\n## Notes / scope decisions\n\n- I kept this **frontend-only**. I checked the API: room-type and rate-plan routes expose only `POST`/`PATCH` — t