          "content": "Everything is coherent and verified. Here's a summary of what I built.\n\n## Delete functionality (backend — new, robust, cascade-safe)\n\nAdded three `DELETE` handlers that follow the exact patterns of the existing POST/PATCH routes (same `withApiHandler`, `propertyOwner` auth, Firestore batch, `enqueueProjection`, `invalidatePublic`):\n\n- **Rate plan** (`rate-plans/[ratePlanId]`): verifies ownership + that the rate belongs to the property, then deletes.\n- **Room type** (`room-types/[roomTypeId]`): **cascades** — deletes all rate plans linked to that room in the same batch, so no orphaned rates break search projections. Returns `removedRatePlans` count.\n- **Cancellation policy** (new file `cancellation-policies/[policyId]/route.ts`): **referential guard** — refuses deletion (422 with a clear message) if any rate still references it, and removes the id from `property.cancellationPolicyIds` in the batch.\n\nAll three validate the child document actually belongs to `propertyId` before touching it, and invalidate public caches.\n\n## Delete functionality (frontend)\n\n- A single `remove(kind, id, label)` handler with a native confirm dialog (cascade warning for rooms), per-item busy state (`deletingId`), automatic reload, and error surfacing via the notice banner.\n- Clears any stale room/policy selection so the rate form never points at a deleted item.\n- Delete buttons (`IconButton`) on every room card, every rate row, and every policy card — with spinner while deleting.\n\n## UI polish — replaced the AI-looking green ticks\n\n- The checklist and accordion steps no longer use generic green check circles. They now use **contextual Lucide icons** in rounded-square tiles: `BedDouble` for room type, `ShieldCheck` for cancellation policy, `Tag` for rate. Active/complete states are conveyed with the brand navy fill rather than a checkmark.\n- Detail cards get matching icon tiles; the \"Added\" pill uses a subtle `BadgeCheck`. Cleaner, more professional, less templated.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean.\n- ESLint on all 4 edited/created files: 0 errors (2 warnings are pre-existing and unrelated — `ImageIcon` and an `<img>` in the photo step).\n- `vitest run`: 7/7 pass.\n\nNote on testing scope: the project has no Firestore-mocking harness for full route integration tests, so I did not fabricate one. The DELETE handlers reuse the same verified building blocks as the existing create/update routes in the same files. If you'd like, I can add a route-level test harness (mocking `adminDb`/`propertyOwner`) as a follow-up.\n\nOne consideration to flag: deletes are **hard deletes** on `roomTypes`/`ratePlans`/`cancellationPolicies`. That's appropriate for the draft onboarding flow, but if you later allow editing a *live* listing, you may want soft-delete (a `deletedAt` flag) there to preserve booking history references — that would be a separate change on the dashboard side.",
